    "answer": {
      "short": "The final term should be $(-1)^n\\binom{n}{n}x^n$: positive when $n$ is even and negative when $n$ is odd.",
      "worked": "In the binomial expansion, the term containing $x^r$ is $\\binom{n}{r}(-x)^r$. For the final term,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{n}{n}(-x)^n&=(-1)^n\\binom{n}{n}x^n.\\end{align*}$$\nIts sign is positive for even $n$ and negative for odd $n$. The printed positive final term is therefore incorrect when $n$ is odd.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
